# Ticket 97: the balance cell cache is a build artifact, keyed on the engine hash.
docs/balance/.cell-cache*.json

# Ticket 42: the desktop wrapper's outputs. `desktop/app/` is a copy of `dist/` and
# `desktop/release/` is the packaged build — both are regenerated by `npm run desktop:build`, and
# `release/` is hundreds of MB of Electron. `desktop/` is its own npm project, so its lockfile is
# ignored for the same reason the root one is never committed.
desktop/app/
desktop/release/
desktop/package-lock.json

# Agent transfer scratch (Henry, 2026-09-11: "move the .tar and .tgz files to _delete").
#
# Sessions move files between this repo and the cloud workspace as tarballs, and staged copies of
# ticket text land beside them. Every one of those is a COPY of something that is either already in
# the tree or on its way in - the four `_sync/*.md` swept up on 09-11 were all already filed, and
# one was a stale fork of its ticket (it still said 151 after the 152 renumber, which is exactly the
# failure mode: a second copy that drifts). None of it belongs in history, and `_tree.tar` alone was
# 41 MB.
#
# `_to_delete/` is ignored too: it is the bin this repo uses because the device mount forbids
# unlink, so things are moved there to be removed by hand rather than deleted in place.
_sync/
_to_delete/
_*.tar
_*.tgz
